1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,900
“Bhai, tilak ka thaal ready hai.
Aa rahe ho na?” Seen 11:02.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,407
Kabir typed a reply…
and deleted it.

3
00:00:07,929 --> 00:00:10,860
No leave in Bengaluru. And one
thought on loop:

4
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:13,809
a call will feel awkward.
Does she even care?

5
00:00:13,809 --> 00:00:16,568
So: call her… or the
‘busy tha yaar’ text?

6
00:00:16,568 --> 00:00:22,519
A 2022 study: 13 experiments, more
than 5,900 people.

7
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:24,705
People sent a ‘just because’ note
to someone they’d lost touch with,

8
00:00:24,705 --> 00:00:26,268
and guessed how much it
would be appreciated.

9
00:00:26,268 --> 00:00:29,358
Then they asked the people who got
it. Again and again…

10
00:00:29,358 --> 00:00:31,369
the senders underestimated.

11
00:00:31,369 --> 00:00:34,866
Why? For the receiver, the big
thing is the surprise: ‘Arre,

12
00:00:34,866 --> 00:00:38,445
he remembered me!’ The more
unexpected, the bigger the gap.

13
00:00:38,445 --> 00:00:42,517
Tradition holds that on this day
Yama visited his sister Yamuna.

14
00:00:42,517 --> 00:00:44,845
Even Yamraj found the time, bhai.

15
00:00:44,845 --> 00:00:48,300
So Kabir skipped the long text.
Straight to video call:

16
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:52,302
“Put the tilak on the screen. Next
year, I bring the thaal.”

17
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:58,870
Atharvaveda 3.30.3: Let not
brother hate brother, nor sister
sister…

18
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:02,193
United, speak your words kindly.

19
00:01:02,193 --> 00:01:05,584
Send this to the
brother who never calls.

20
00:01:05,584 --> 00:01:08,774
This Bhai Dooj: a call, or the
‘busy tha’ text? 1 or 2,

21
00:01:08,774 --> 00:01:11,329
in the comments.
